  "domain": "spatial-computing",
  "definition": "The dominant real-time rendering technique that converts 3D geometric primitives \u2014 predominantly triangles \u2014 into a 2D pixel representation by determining per-pixel coverage, depth, and colour through a GPU-accelerated pipeline of vertex processing, primitive assembly, scan conversion, fragment shading, and output merging. Rasterization trades photorealistic accuracy for deterministic, high-throughput performance suitable for interactive applications.",
